{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 102, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a weak avg_pool with a 3x3 conv gives a much larger gain than replacing skip or other ops (experiments 48, 34)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading an avg_pool on edge 0 to a 3x3 conv gains about 6-10 points, versus 1.5-3.5 when replacing skip_connect."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the direct 0->3 edge is catastrophic when edge 4 is also absent, since the output loses its main paths."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a conv on the final edge with avg_pool loses 3-7 points, more than replacing a skip."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping the direct skip on edge 3 for avg_pool costs several points (experiments 8, 83)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning a skip on edge 2 into a 3x3 conv adds capacity and gains more than refining an existing conv or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a strong 3x3 conv on edge 1 with avg_pool removes learned capacity (experiment 17)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip on edge 3 helps most when edge 4 is absent and the output has few other paths (experiments 25, 24)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a pooling ed